Upstream gap: Open WebUI keeps only id and name from a manifold Pipe's
pipes() entries and reads a model's description, capabilities, default tools,
Filters, and Chat Variables form only from a stored model record, so a Pipe
cannot describe the models it lists (open-webui#23047, declined upstream).

Keep the info dict of each pipes() entry as the listed model's info, the shape
a stored model record provides. A stored record for the same model still
replaces it.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release that keeps model info from pipes().
--- a/open_webui/functions.py
+++ b/open_webui/functions.py
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@
                             'owned_by': 'openai',
                             'pipe': pipe_flag,
                             'has_user_valves': has_user_valves,
+                            **({'info': p['info']} if 'info' in p else {}),
                         }
                     )
             else:
